---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Inflation Cheat Sheet | Free Exponential Expansion, Horizon Problem, Flatness"
  description="Complete inflation cheat sheet with exponential expansion, horizon problem, and flatness. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Inflation<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Exponential expansion, horizon problem, and flatness. From Big Bang to quantum fluctuations.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Problems Solved</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Horizon Problem</h3>
        <pre><code>CMB is uniform across sky
But regions were never in causal contact
Inflation: exponential expansion before CMB
Regions were in contact, then expanded apart</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Flatness Problem</h3>
        <pre><code>Universe is very flat (Ω ≈ 1)
Without inflation: fine-tuning required
Inflation: exponential expansion drives Ω → 1
Any curvature is diluted away</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Magnetic Monopole Problem</h3>
        <pre><code>GUT predicts many monopoles
None observed
Inflation: monopoles diluted to unobservable density</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Inflationary Dynamics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Exponential Expansion</h3>
        <pre><code>a(t) = a₀ exp(Ht) (de Sitter space)
H = const during inflation
e-folds: N = ln(a_end/a_start) > 60
Duration: t ~ 10⁻³⁶ to 10⁻³² s</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Slow-Roll Inflation</h3>
        <pre><code>Inflaton field: φ rolling slowly down potential
Slow-roll parameters: ε, η << 1
ε = -Ḣ/H² (kinetic energy << potential)
η = V''/V (potential is flat)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Predictions</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Observational Signatures</h3>
        <pre><code>Nearly scale-invariant spectrum: n_s ≈ 0.965
Small tensor-to-scalar ratio: r < 0.1
Gaussian fluctuations
Adiabatic perturbations
Spatial flatness</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>End of Inflation</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Reheating</h3>
        <pre><code>Inflaton oscillates around minimum
Decays into Standard Model particles
Reheats universe to T ~ 10¹⁵ GeV
Begins Hot Big Bang</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
